<% /* "Embed item" control. Single source of truth — included by the media card of
      the standard, grid, and timeline item forms (every media type: an embedded item
      of any type opens in place, never in the pop-up viewer). On add/edit media forms
      helperModule.bind_embed_description moves #embed-item-group to directly ABOVE the
      Pop-up Window Description field and disables that editor — with a note under its
      label — while this box is checked. The description is kept, not cleared: search
      results and the search index still read it. */ %>
<div id="embed-item-group" class="form-group" style="padding-top: 10px">
    <small class="form-text text-muted"><i class="fa fa-exclamation-circle" aria-hidden="true"></i> <em>Embedded items do not open the item viewer (pop-up window)</em></small>
    <label for="embed-item" style="font-weight: normal; cursor: pointer">Embed item&nbsp;<input type="checkbox" id="embed-item" name="embed_item"></label>
</div>
